# Tests get their configuration from phpunit.xml, which sets every variable the
# suite needs with force="true" and repeats them as <server> entries. Nothing
# belongs in here.
#
# The file exists so Laravel has an environment file to find. APP_ENV=testing
# points its bootstrap at this one instead of .env, which is gitignored and so
# absent in CI — and a missing env file becomes a PHP warning that PHPUnit
# attributes to every test that boots the application.
